IMPORT prelude

-- Mental Capacity Act 2008 (Singapore) -- the principles, the test of capacity, best interests, the protection for
-- acts of care and treatment and its limits on restraint, the decisions no one may make for another, and the
-- ill-treatment offence: ss 3 to 8, 26, 28 and 42.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 34 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository (s 4 by 9, s 2 by 5). It is the Act a
-- family meets when a parent develops dementia. SCOPED to capacity, care, lasting powers of attorney and deputies'
-- limits. Not encoded: payment for necessaries and expenditure (ss 9, 10), the electronic system (Part 3A), the court's
-- powers and deputies' appointment except their limits (Part 5), the Public Guardian and Board of Visitors (Part 7),
-- court procedure (Part 8), and most of Part 9.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Mental Capacity Act 2008 -- capacity and care`

§§ `3, 4, 5 -- who lacks capacity`

-- s 3(2): "A person must be assumed to have capacity unless it is established that the person lacks capacity." (3): not
-- unable "unless all practicable steps to help the person to do so have been taken without success". (4): not unable
-- "merely because the person makes an unwise decision".
-- s 4(1): a person lacks capacity in relation to a matter if at the material time they are unable to decide it "because
-- of an impairment of, or a disturbance in the functioning of, the mind or brain"; (2) permanent or temporary; (3) not
-- established merely by age, appearance, a condition or behaviour.
-- s 5(1): unable to decide if unable "(a) to understand the information relevant to the decision; (b) to retain that
-- information; (c) to use or weigh that information ...; or (d) to communicate" it. (2): able to understand an
-- appropriate explanation counts as understanding. (3): retaining it "for a short period only" does not prevent capacity.
-- s 4(5): no power under the Act is exercisable in relation to a person below 21 YEARS (subject to s 21).
--
-- Capacity is decision-specific and time-specific; the four abilities are alternatives (any one missing is enough); and
-- the impairment must be the cause.
DECLARE Assessment HAS
    `has an impairment or disturbance of mind or brain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `understands the relevant information, with appropriate explanation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `retains it, even briefly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `uses or weighs it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `communicates a decision by any means` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all practicable steps to help were taken` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the decision is unwise` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the assessment` IS AN Assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is unable to make the decision` IF
        NOT `the assessment`'s `understands the relevant information, with appropriate explanation`
    OR  NOT `the assessment`'s `retains it, even briefly`
    OR  NOT `the assessment`'s `uses or weighs it`
    OR  NOT `the assessment`'s `communicates a decision by any means`

GIVEN `the assessment` IS AN Assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person lacks capacity for the decision` IF
        `the assessment`'s `has an impairment or disturbance of mind or brain`
    AND `the person is unable to make the decision` `the assessment`
    AND `the assessment`'s `all practicable steps to help were taken`

-- An unwise decision is never itself proof of incapacity.
GIVEN `the assessment` IS AN Assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unwise decision alone shows incapacity` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act's powers may be exercised for the person` IF
    `age` AT LEAST 21

§§ `6 -- best interests`

-- s 6(1): not merely on age, appearance, condition or behaviour. (3): whether the person will regain capacity. (4):
-- encourage participation. (5): on life-sustaining treatment, the decider "must not ... be motivated by a desire to bring
-- about the death". (7): on the disposition or settlement of the person's PROPERTY, the decider "must be motivated by a
-- desire to ensure, so far as is reasonably practicable, that the person's property is PRESERVED for application towards
-- the costs of the person's maintenance during the person's life". (8): past and present wishes, beliefs and values.
-- (9): consult carers, donees and deputies. (11): for anyone but the court, compliance is sufficient if, having done all
-- that, the decider "reasonably believes" the act is in the person's best interests.
--
-- s 6(7) points property decisions at preserving the estate for the person's own care -- which tells against selling the
-- family home to fund a child's purchase, even one the parent would once have wanted.
DECLARE BestInterests HAS
    `considered whether capacity may return` IS A BOOLEAN
    `encouraged participation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `considered past and present wishes, beliefs and values` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consulted carers, donees and deputies where practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `decided merely on age, appearance or condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `motivated by a desire to bring about death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a property decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `aimed to preserve the property for the person's own maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonably believes it is in the person's best interests` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the decision` IS A BestInterests
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision complies with section 6` IF
        `the decision`'s `considered whether capacity may return`
    AND `the decision`'s `encouraged participation`
    AND `the decision`'s `considered past and present wishes, beliefs and values`
    AND `the decision`'s `consulted carers, donees and deputies where practicable`
    AND NOT `the decision`'s `decided merely on age, appearance or condition`
    AND NOT `the decision`'s `motivated by a desire to bring about death`
    AND (    NOT `the decision`'s `is a property decision`
         OR  `the decision`'s `aimed to preserve the property for the person's own maintenance`)
    AND `the decision`'s `reasonably believes it is in the person's best interests`

§§ `7, 8 -- protection for acts of care and treatment`

-- s 7(1), (2): a carer or clinician who, BEFORE acting, takes reasonable steps to establish whether P lacks capacity, and
-- WHEN acting reasonably believes P lacks capacity and the act is in P's best interests, incurs no liability they would not
-- have incurred had P consented. (3)(a): but not for NEGLIGENCE in doing the act.
-- s 8(1) to (4): an act intended to RESTRAIN P -- using or threatening force against resistance, or restricting liberty of
-- movement "whether or not P resists" -- is protected only if D reasonably believes it necessary to prevent harm to P AND
-- it is a proportionate response to the likelihood and seriousness of the harm. (5): not against a valid decision of a
-- donee or deputy.
DECLARE CareAct HAS
    `took reasonable steps to establish capacity beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonably believed P lacked capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonably believed it was in P's best interests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a restraint` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonably believed it necessary to prevent harm to P` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proportionate to the likelihood and seriousness of harm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contrary to a valid decision of a donee or deputy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `done negligently` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the act` IS A CareAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is protected by section 7` IF
        `the act`'s `took reasonable steps to establish capacity beforehand`
    AND `the act`'s `reasonably believed P lacked capacity`
    AND `the act`'s `reasonably believed it was in P's best interests`
    AND NOT `the act`'s `contrary to a valid decision of a donee or deputy`
    AND (    NOT `the act`'s `is a restraint`
         OR  (    `the act`'s `reasonably believed it necessary to prevent harm to P`
              AND `the act`'s `proportionate to the likelihood and seriousness of harm`))

GIVEN `the act` IS A CareAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor may still be liable in negligence` IF
    `the act`'s `done negligently`

§§ `26, 28 -- decisions no one may make for another`

-- s 26: "Nothing in this Act permits a decision on any of the following matters to be made on behalf of a person: (a)
-- consenting to marriage; (b) consenting to touching of a sexual nature; (c) consenting to a divorce on 3 years'
-- separation; (d) adoption; (e) adopting or renouncing a RELIGION; (f) treatment for change of gender; (g) sterilisation;
-- (h) termination of pregnancy; (i) an organ-transplant objection; (j) an advance medical directive; (k) a gift of the
-- body". s 28: voting at an election or referendum.
DECLARE Matter IS ONE OF
    `marriage`
    `sexual touching`
    `divorce on 3 years' separation`
    `adoption`
    `religion`
    `gender reassignment`
    `sterilisation`
    `termination of pregnancy`
    `an organ-transplant objection`
    `an advance medical directive`
    `a gift of the body`
    `voting`
    `selling the home`
    `choosing a care home`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `selling the home` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `choosing a care home` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `42 -- ill-treatment`

-- s 42(1): applies to a person who has the CARE of P, is P's donee, or is P's deputy, "and P is 16 YEARS of age or
-- above". (3), (4): ill-treatment includes physical or sexual abuse, wilful or unreasonable endangering, and wilful or
-- unreasonable neglect to provide food, clothing, medical aid, lodging or care. (5): no defence that another person
-- prevented the harm. (6): where death is caused, $40,000 or 14 YEARS; otherwise $8,000 or 8 years.
--
-- The offence protects a person from 16; the rest of the Act's powers start at 21 (s 4(5)). A 17-year-old who lacks
-- capacity is protected by s 42 but cannot have an LPA donee or, outside s 21, a deputy under this Act.
DECLARE IllTreatment HAS
    `D cares for P, or is P's donee or deputy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `P's age` IS A NUMBER
    `abused, endangered or neglected P wilfully or unreasonably` IS A BOOLEAN
    `P died` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN IllTreatment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `D commits the ill-treatment offence` IF
        `the facts`'s `D cares for P, or is P's donee or deputy`
    AND `the facts`'s `P's age` AT LEAST 16
    AND `the facts`'s `abused, endangered or neglected P wilfully or unreasonably`

-- In years.
GIVEN `the facts` IS AN IllTreatment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment for ill-treatment` MEANS
    IF `the facts`'s `P died` THEN 14 ELSE 8
